---
import Quiz from './Quiz.astro';
---
<section id="gait" class="rex-section" aria-labelledby="gait-title" data-gait-lab>
  <div class="rex-section-heading"><p class="rex-eyebrow">03 / Kinematics instrument</p><h2 id="gait-title">Draw a step. Solve a leg.</h2><p>The foot has a destination. The joints need angles. Inverse kinematics connects the two — here, with just two equal links and a flat foot.</p></div>
  <div class="rex-instrument">
    <div class="rex-instrument-bar"><span>GAIT WORKBENCH</span><span>SIMPLIFIED EDUCATIONAL MODEL</span></div>
    <div class="rex-lab-layout">
      <div class="rex-plot">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 500 390" role="img" aria-labelledby="gait-svg-title gait-svg-desc"><title id="gait-svg-title">A two-link leg follows an editable foot path</title><desc id="gait-svg-desc">A dashed curve is the target trajectory. The leg is solved analytically. A readout indicates targets beyond the leg’s reach.</desc><defs><pattern id="gait-grid" width="25" height="25" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M25 0H0V25" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width=".5" opacity=".15" /></pattern></defs><rect x="25" y="20" width="450" height="340" fill="url(#gait-grid)" /><path data-gait-floor d="M40 330H460" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" /><path data-gait-path fill="none" stroke="var(--rex-accent)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 4" /><path d="M214 43h72v25h-72z" fill="var(--wash)" stroke="currentColor" /><path data-gait-leg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="13" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path data-gait-foot stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="7" /><g data-gait-joints fill="var(--paper)" stroke="var(--rex-accent)" stroke-width="3"></g><circle data-gait-target r="6" fill="var(--rex-accent)" /><text x="35" y="42" class="rex-svg-label">SIDE VIEW</text><text x="35" y="380" class="rex-svg-label">ILLUSTRATIVE LINKS / 80 + 80 mm</text><text x="400" y="42" class="rex-svg-label">FORWARD →</text></svg>
        <div class="rex-readouts rex-gait-readouts"><div><span>Phase</span><strong data-gait-mode>Stance</strong></div><div><span>Hip / knee / ankle</span><strong data-gait-angles>0° / 0° / 0°</strong></div></div>
        <p class="rex-reach-status" data-gait-reach aria-live="polite">Target reachable in this two-link model.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rex-control-panel">
        <div class="rex-control-actions"><button type="button" data-gait-play aria-pressed="false">Play cycle</button><button type="button" data-gait-reset>Reset gait</button></div>
        <label class="rex-slider-label" for="gait-phase">Cycle phase <output for="gait-phase" data-phase-value>0%</output></label><input id="gait-phase" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="0" step="0.1" />
        <label class="rex-slider-label" for="gait-stride">Step length <output for="gait-stride" data-stride-value>50 mm</output></label><input id="gait-stride" type="range" min="10" max="90" value="50" step="1" />
        <label class="rex-slider-label" for="gait-lift">Foot lift <output for="gait-lift" data-lift-value>25 mm</output></label><input id="gait-lift" type="range" min="0" max="50" value="25" step="1" />
        <label class="rex-slider-label" for="gait-height">Hip height <output for="gait-height" data-height-value>125 mm</output></label><input id="gait-height" type="range" min="100" max="175" value="125" step="1" />
        <p class="rex-caption">One cycle = 62% stance + 38% swing; playback = 0.5 cycles/s. The hip is fixed. No balance controller, servo constraints, loads or ground-contact solver. Scrubbing pauses playback. Motion starts only when you press Play.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="rex-teaching"><p><strong>Stance:</strong> the foot moves backward relative to the fixed hip. On a walking robot with a planted foot, the body would move forward. <strong>Swing:</strong> the foot lifts and returns. The ankle angle keeps the drawn foot level.</p><p><strong>Try this:</strong> raise hip height to 175 mm. Two 80 mm links cannot reach that far. The solver clamps the drawn leg; the target stays visible. A longer step is not automatically a feasible step.</p></div>
  <details class="rex-details"><summary>Under the instrument / the two-link solution</summary><div><p>For target (x, y) relative to the hip and link lengths a and b: cos(knee) = (x² + y² − a² − b²) / (2ab). Then hip = atan2(x, y) − atan2(b sin(knee), a + b cos(knee)). The sketch uses downward-positive y and ankle = −hip − knee.</p><p>Targets beyond the reachable annulus are projected onto it. “Reachable” means geometrically reachable for this toy linkage only — not collision-free, balanced or within the native robot’s joint limits.</p></div></details>
  <Quiz id="gait-quiz" question="A foot path is reachable. Have we proved the robot can walk it?" choices={['Not yet — balance, contacts, torque and limits still matter.', 'Yes — the inverse kinematics solution is enough.']} answer={0} explanation="Kinematics solves geometry. Walking also needs dynamics, sufficient torque, reliable contacts, joint limits and feedback — then physical validation." />
</section>
